WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.904
This paper makes three main contributions.

00:00:03.984 --> 00:00:07.888
First, it proposes TimeSiam,

00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:11.872
a simple but effective pre-training framework that
uses Siamese networks to capture correlations

00:00:11.953 --> 00:00:15.857
among temporally distanced subseries.

00:00:15.937 --> 00:00:19.841
Second, it introduces learnable lineage embeddings,

00:00:19.921 --> 00:00:23.825
a lightweight mechanism that lets one model
represent many different past-to-current time distances.

00:00:23.905 --> 00:00:27.809
Third,

00:00:27.889 --> 00:00:31.793
through extensive experiments it shows TimeSiam
achieves consistent state-of-the-art results

00:00:31.873 --> 00:00:35.778
when fine-tuned on both forecasting and classification,

00:00:35.858 --> 00:00:39.762
and across both in-domain and cross-domain settings.

00:00:39.842 --> 00:00:43.746
Crucially, the framework is backbone-agnostic,

00:00:43.826 --> 00:00:47.730
dropping cleanly onto modern encoders like
iTransformer, PatchTST, and TCN.
